A||||21||MD_Fiero||burnouts.. =)...||||1||
Z||000000||MD_Fiero||07-31-2001||12:03 PM||||Who here can tell me how to do a burnout, with my fiero, i have tried it many times, but no, it just sticks to the ground! errr!!<P>im not trying to do a nuetral drop...burning is mad easy in the rain, but i dont want to do it in the rain =) thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||07-31-2001||12:11 PM||||Well...I've got a hot 3.1L in my '87 GT and I'm in about the same boat. It ALWAYS hooks up (like you said...unless it's wet)! I did  a little research- and this is only if you're totally serious about burnouts. Check with summit racing for a "Line Lock" system. It's a relay that allows you to lock only the front brakes.  This allows you to floor it and not have any brake pressure on the back.  Keep in mind that this is a good way to destroy tires!  Hope this helps.<BR>-Rob||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||07-31-2001||12:29 PM||||The only way you will get an auto to do a burn out is get a really built motor, or get a high stall converter.  Minngreengt is correct that a line lock will work, but I am always worried anytime it concenrs plumbing a valve into a braking system.  When my car was an auto. (85GT 2.8 Auto very high milage) I did everything in my power to make the tires spin, I eventully found that a bit of tranny fluid would make em spin, but that would be for exibition purposes only.   If you really want to get the tires roasting your best bet is to get a stick shift fiero. I can safly say I can lite the tires up with the best of them now, (2.9 4spd to many mods to list)<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tryxalon||07-31-2001||12:38 PM||||Why would you want to? <P>Fiero's mid-engine design is optimal for maximizing traction and putting torque to the ground. (even with a manual)<P>"Burn outs" waste fuel, tire tread and time to no useful effect. <P>Besides, IMHO it looks really stupid to have your tires rotating rapidly while your car is not moving ... kinda like the coyote after the road runner has just "dusted" him.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000004||KRMFiero||07-31-2001||12:54 PM||||Get a 5 speed, youll light them up like nothing, do you have the duke or the 2.8? i know my 2.5 auto never could spin them but with the 5 speed it will all day long||||reg||1
