Z||000009||87FieroGTx||07-31-2001||03:50 PM|||| Oh If you want to burnout turn left and floor it)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Capt Fiero||07-31-2001||03:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tryxalon:<BR><B>Why would you want to? <P><BR>"Burn outs" waste fuel, tire tread and time to no useful effect. <P>Besides, IMHO it looks really stupid to have your tires rotating rapidly while your car is not moving ... kinda like the coyote after the road runner has just "dusted" him.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I guess you are not into drag racing then, to get the fieros best launch possible it requrires you to spin the tires a little, when I say a little I do not mean a 20ft smoke show either.  I get my best 0-60 with a clutch dump at about 4500 letting the rpms drop to about 3000 as the tires spin it keeps the car in the power band and when it does hook the car pulls a lot harder through 1st gear.  If you try to launch a standerd or an auto you want the rpms to be about 3500 or you will just bog out of the hole.  That is why they invented high rpm stall converters. And please dont reply and tell me to slip the clutch slipping the cluch for one is really hard on it, and 2nd when slipping the clutch that hard you are wasting energy that is not producing forward momentuim.  Becuase of the Fiero's great traction even doing a big burnout the car is still pulling forward really quick. Hence the pic in my sig, look at how far the marks (yes marks x 2) go behind my car and that was about a 4500rpm drop.<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||07-31-2001||05:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B> [TROLL]And a completely useless engine.[/TROLL]   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Still feeling threatend Steve?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"And God said there shall be one in thy owns image, and he made me"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||07-31-2001||10:05 PM||||If thats your thing. But its lots easier on the equipment to not do it. No blown clutches, no busted axles, no busted trannys. But to each there own. When the mustang or camaro is smoking his tires looking cool, im gone...usually a hundred yards ahead. I had my tire smoking days too........when i was 18. That runs in the same mentality to me as smacking your wife/gf cause you want to.<BR>||||reg||1
